# Keep the build context lean so `COPY src/ src/` in Dockerfile.collector
# doesn't sweep in hundreds of MB of dev artifacts. The collector image
# itself only needs five Python files under src/mycelium/, but the
# `pip install --no-deps .` step needs the full package tree on disk —
# we just don't want it carrying ballast.
#
# Measured impact at the time of writing:
#   - src/mycelium/adapters/openclaw/.../node_modules: 543 MB
#   - .venv:                                          219 MB
#   - build/:                                           2.5 MB
#   - tests/:                                           0.2 MB
# Reducing the `COPY src/` layer from ~545 MB to ~2 MB also reduces
# build context transfer time on every rebuild.

# ── Local Python environments (never belong in an image) ────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.tox/

# ── Bytecode and caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ty_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ── Node tooling for the OpenClaw plugin (543 MB!) ──────────────────
# The plugin's runtime dist/ stays; node_modules is dev-only and is
# already excluded from the wheel via `[tool.setuptools.exclude-package-data]`
# in pyproject.toml. We need the same exclusion at COPY time.
**/node_modules/
**/package-lock.json

# Plugin unit tests and IDE config — no runtime purpose
**/plugin/test/
**/plugin/.vitest/

# ── VCS / IDE / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# ── Docs / changelogs (not used at runtime by the collector) ────────
docs/
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
LICENSE
